        {
          "text": "HUANG Fang-shih 黃芳世 (T. 周士), d. 1678, general, was a native of P'ing-ho, Fukien. When his uncle, Huang Wu [q. v.], was in command of the troops at Chang-chou, Huang Fang-shih represented him at Court, received preferment, and for twelve years enjoyed the life of Peking.",
          "source": "eccp-3640007",
          "kind": "source-wording",
          "status": "imported"
        }
